  "id": "chemical-synapse",
  "term": "chemical synapse",
  "definition": "A chemical synapse is a junction between cells where an electrical signal in the presynaptic cell triggers release of a neurotransmitter. The neurotransmitter crosses the synaptic gap and binds to ion channels on the postsynaptic cell, changing that cell’s resting electrical state.",
